{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MtoGyiuqeC26S7mbpNGyE2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's my plan:\n\n**Vite Plugin** (`vitePlugin.js`): Currently the SSR middleware loads a single entrypoint and calls `render(name, props, slots)`. For multi-framework support, the Elixir side already knows the framework (it sets `data-framework=\"vue\"`). The ViteJS SSR module sends `{name, props, slots}` — we need to also accept a `framework` field so the SSR endpoint can route to the correct renderer. The plugin should support multiple entrypoints (one per framework) or a single entrypoint that exports per-framework render functions.\n\n**Server.ts**: Add a `getMultiRendererRender()` function that takes a map of `RendererEntry` objects (matching the hooks pattern) and returns a render function that dispatches by framework name.\n\nLet me start with the Vite plugin."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":298,"cache_read_input_tokens":45205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":298},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d3f72d8-93a7-4fae-b97c-2962753cba3f","uuid":"c6149f0e-1e4b-42d3-8ca1-3845d1c45143"}
