{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018UHjqi44a6ov5A8qSgVfG6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — `server.ts` is exported as a separate entry point (`live_vite/server`), not through `index.ts`. The `getMultiRendererRender` is already available via `import { getMultiRendererRender } from \"live_vite/server\"`. No changes needed to `index.ts` for server exports.\n\nHowever, I should verify that `RendererEntry` is properly importable. Let me check if `RendererEntry` needs to be re-exported from server.ts or if the import from hooks.ts is sufficient.\n\nActually, looking at the import in server.ts — I'm importing `RendererEntry` from `./hooks.js`. That's fine since users already import `RendererEntry` from `live_vite` (it's exported in index.ts). The server.ts module just needs the type internally.\n\nLet me also check that the Elixir side sends a `framework` field in the SSR request. Currently it doesn't, but the Vite plugin change is backward-compatible — if `framework` is undefined, `getMultiRendererRender` falls back to the single renderer.\n\nNow let me also update the Elixir ViteJS SSR module to pass the framework name. Let me check the NodeJS one too."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1173,"cache_read_input_tokens":52216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1173},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d3f72d8-93a7-4fae-b97c-2962753cba3f","uuid":"cebf4cc9-8fe5-43da-bf90-5915e79559ae"}
