{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VmLLmwAnViwGUKTzPKWTLh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `__framework` value is set once during init and won't change during the lifecycle, so it doesn't need special change tracking. The `data-framework` attribute using `{@__framework}` will be included in initial renders just fine.\n\nNow let me update the exports. The `getMultiRendererRender` is already exported from `server.ts` which has its own entry point in package.json. Let me verify the `index.ts` doesn't need changes for the server function — it doesn't since server.ts is a separate entry point.\n\nBut I should export `getMultiRendererRender` from `index.ts` as well for discoverability, since users might import from the main entry point.\n\nActually, looking at the pattern — `getRender`, `getRendererRender`, and `loadManifest` are only in `server.ts` and NOT in `index.ts`. This is because they're server-only (they import `fs`, `vue/server-renderer`, etc.). So `getMultiRendererRender` should follow the same pattern — only exported from `server.ts`. No changes to `index.ts` needed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":652,"cache_read_input_tokens":66315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":652},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d3f72d8-93a7-4fae-b97c-2962753cba3f","uuid":"fb2e54e8-8d66-4962-bc0f-8a916b516f96"}
